cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Marlo or its calibration tables in research, please cite it with
  the metadata below, and name the commit on main the numbers came from.
  Every published figure is regenerated from calibration/table.json, which
  records the engine versions and the corpus date it was measured with.
type: software
title: 'Marlo: multi-engine accessibility testing with a published error rate'
abstract: >-
  Marlo runs several accessibility engines against a page and routes each
  W3C ACT rule to the engine with the best measured accuracy on the ACT
  Rules Community test cases. Precision, recall and the false positive rate
  for every rule and engine are measured, published, and checked on every
  change, together with results on two corpora of real pages.
authors:
  - family-names: Subramanian
    given-names: Karthik
repository-code: 'https://github.com/KarthikSubramanian07/Marlo'
url: 'https://trymarlo.pages.dev'
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - WCAG
  - ACT rules
  - static analysis
  - axe-core
  - calibration
